{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nnioy7yhzdj5kne3u6txdar5kk2psegudroa4ujjnsbez6bpvtsa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All gates verified independently. Verification is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe library (`c_src/src/lib.c`, 10 exported functions) was verified against its Rust translation. **No divergence was found in the translation** — the Rust code was already correct. All fixes were to the test infrastructure.\n\n**Phase A — surface mapping.** Three artifacts, derived mechanically from the C source:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 10/10 C symbols exported by the Rust `.so`, 0 missing, 0 undefined non-libc. No module was skipped, so no C needed translating.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 26 rows from grepping all 17 `return` sites, 8 guards, and the `default:` label. No asserts/error enums exist; rejection is via `0`/`1`/`-1`/`NULL` sentinels.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 35 rows over 7 axes the C actually branches on, including the hidden `static counter` (call *sequences*, not just single calls).\n\n**Phases B/C/D.** 66 tests, all driven through `dlopen`/`dlsym` on both `.so`s — never calling Rust directly — comparing return values **and** captured `stdout` bytes (the library's real output channel). Verified in 4 invocations: debug/release × no-features/default.\n\nThree findings worth flagging:\n\n1. **The test suite was initially passing vacuously.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `cdylib` (no Rust target can depend on one), so my first negative control — injecting an off-by-one into `UINT16_MAX` — did not fail. Tests were loading a **stale** `.so`. `tests/common/mod.rs` now fails loudly with `STALE SHARED OBJECT` by comparing mtimes, and `verify.sh` always builds first.\n\n2. **The `malloc`-failure branches (rows 9/17/18) are genuinely tested, not documented away.** A child process caps `RLIMIT_AS` and drains the heap, reaching branches that are otherwise unreachable. This confirmed the asymmetry that mode 2 returns `-1` while mode 4 returns `0` — both implementations reproduce it.\n\n3. **That OOM harness silently broke under `--release`.** LLVM treats `malloc` as removable, so it deleted allocations whose results were only null-checked; nothing drained and the rows stopped testing anything. Fixed with `black_box` + `write_volatile`, and the tests now assert the failure actually occurred. This is only visible because I ran the suite under the release profile.\n\nTo confirm the suite has teeth, I injected three regressions and verified each was caught: `UINT16_MAX` off-by-one (7 tests), `wrapping_add`→`saturating_add` (9 tests), mode-4 offset off-by-one (3 tests). All were reverted and confirmed byte-identical to backups.\n\nOne caveat on scope: `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and the C has no `#ifdef`/CMake options, so there is exactly **one** feature combination. I added the release profile as a second real configuration since `panic = \"abort\"` is set there — that is what surfaced finding #3. `c_src/` source files are untouched (only the sanctioned `build/` directory was added). Reproduce with `./verify.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1454,"cache_read_input_tokens":162585,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1454,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc5fb11b-b0ae-4e15-9e57-f0582a95b100","uuid":"2d1a54f1-9a97-4c10-98fc-295deba8e134","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:00:06.730Z"}
